{
  "about": "The cast's Hyper3D Rodin parts (T81) as Unreal assets (T82 prep, 2026-11-15). Each fit is a relative transform for a component under its parent in BP_Robot (Rig, or ArmPivotL/ArmPivotR for the arms), in cm, Rig +X = the robot's face, Z up, floor z 0. Rotations are UE (roll, pitch, yaw) in degrees. 'offset' is the component's relative location (arms: relative to the pivot). See Docs/tasks/T82-build.md.",
  "frame": "Every Rodin part faces mesh +Y after import (the importer maps raw (x, y, z) to (100x, -100y, 100z) cm), so yaw 270 (= -90) turns its front to Rig +X. Bent arms add a roll that hangs them straight down. A mirrored arm has its X scale negated and its rotation mirrored, as given.",
  "material": {
    "master": "/Game/NHOS/Stage/Materials/M_CastModel",
    "parameters": {
      "BaseTex": "texture",
      "NormalTex": "texture (normal)",
      "RoughTex": "texture",
      "Color": "vector, default (1,1,1): the seat color; multiplied in by TintAmount",
      "TintAmount": "scalar, default 0 (1 on the white head shell)",
      "Cut": "scalar 0..1, default 0: the cut's gray",
      "GrayFromColor": "scalar, default 0 in the master and 1 in every MI here: a Color with no saturation (SetCut's 0.16 gray) also counts as cut",
      "CutTint": "vector, default (0.25,0.25,0.25): the desaturated texture times this on the cut",
      "Rough": "scalar, default 0.85",
      "RoughFromTex": "scalar, default 0.5",
      "NormalAmount": "scalar, default 1"
    }
  },
  "targets": {
    "head_top_z": 158,
    "round_head_width_cm": 70,
    "label_z": 228,
    "arm_length_cm": 53,
    "hand_centre_in_pivot": [
